cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Natura 2000 site evidence for Kras (SI3000276): grassland, overgrowth and forest from the Slovenian Land Use database, open EU-wide layers and GBIF on WGS84 HEALPix"
abstract: >-
  DRAFT. A monitoring workflow for Natura 2000 sites in Slovenia, piloted on SI3000276 Kras:
  per site, the current extent of permanent grassland, overgrown agricultural land, trees and
  shrubs and forest from the national Land Use database (MKGP RABA), change since the previous
  snapshot and since 2002, and how current the data are. Validated against Davidović, Čuš and
  Ivajnšič (2026). Open EU-wide layers (Article 17, CORINE Land Cover and change, CLC+ Backbone,
  HRL Grassland) and GBIF species records on HEALPix (GRID4EARTH DGGS-Zarr) are compared for the
  same site. Results from the national database are produced locally and not published pending
  permission from MKGP. Not yet reviewed by an ecologist or by the Slovenian Distributed Centre
  of LifeWatch (ZRC SAZU).
